# Player architecture (pointer)

Full law: [`docs/docs/architecture/player.md`](../../docs/docs/architecture/player.md).

**Permanent decision:** one character vitals model — **HP**, **hunger**,
**thirst**, **medication toxicity**. Planet surface applies authored
**temperature** + **breathable air** (may be lethal). Stations / habs /
hangars / ship interiors are sealed (no temp/air stress). Vacuum without a
suit has no air. Medicine heals HP and **adds toxicity**; lethal toxicity
kills; toxicity decays slowly. HUD: hunger / thirst / toxicology always;
planet temp/atmo **only on planet**; HP **only below 100%**. Cell owns
outcomes; client owns HUD. Ship hull vitals stay separate
([Ship combat](../../docs/docs/architecture/ship-combat.md)).

When changing character HP, hunger, thirst, planet life-support stress,
medicine / toxicology, or player HUD vitals visibility, read the full doc
first. Home world offers / signup: [Home Worlds](../../docs/docs/architecture/home-worlds.md).
Death / respawn: [Player death](../../docs/docs/architecture/player-death.md).
Also listed in `AGENTS.md`.
